1. Spring Boot transaction handilng.
     @EnableTransactionManagement - Application level.
     @Transactional - Method level annotation.

2. Spring boot exception handilng.
     @RestControllerAdvice - class level annotation
     @ExceptionHandler - Method level annotation

3. Rest Endpoint communication.
   1. add spring webflux dependency
   2. We can use Webclient which is available in the above dependency to communicate with other server Rest endpoints.
     WebClient.builder().build()
                .get()
                .uri("https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users")
                .retrieve()
                .bodyToMono(String.class)
                .block();
      get() - http method
      uri - URL we goinmg to hit to get response
      retrieve - execute the request
      bodyToMono - the response we received will be mapped to string type
      block - wait until the execution completes.

   For converting response to object we can mention Object.class directly (ex :  bodyToMono(User.class) - converts response to user object))

4. Spring Boot Swagger documentation.
   1. Dependency
     org.springdoc: springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc : 2.6.0
   2. Goto Browser and use the URL( /swagger-ui/index.html)

5. Spring Boot actuaters.
  application Heathcheck - weather my app is up and running or not.  
  metrics - JVM memory, server memory, process config etc  
  1. Dependency
    org.springframework.boot: spring-boot-starter-actuator.
  2. write a config in application.properties
     management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=health,info,metrics
     management.endpoint.health.show-details=always
     
  3. hit the actuator URL. 
    /actuator
    {
  "_links": {
    "self": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/actuator", - Lists you all the actuator URLs 
      "templated": false
    },
    "health-path": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/actuator/health/{*path}",
      "templated": true
    },
    "health": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/actuator/health", - Health check URL
      "templated": false
    },
    "info": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/actuator/info",
      "templated": false
    },
    "metrics-requiredMetricName": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics/{requiredMetricName}", - the key from below URl can be used here to extract corresponding metric values. EX: Processor usage, memory usage, CPU Usage. 
      "templated": true
    },
    "metrics": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/actuator/metrics", - Lists you all the metrics keys that you can query.
      "templated": false
    }
  }